  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>: Two triangles are identical<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>: Two triangles are similar</p><p>Clearly, the given statement in symbolic form is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>q</mi></math>.<br /><br />Contrapositive of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>q</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow> </math><br /><br />i.e., If two triangles are not similar, then they are not identical.</p>",
